{
 "source_notes": "All values from Bowen National Research, '2024 Housing Supply Gap Analysis, State of North Carolina' (same report as the ncchamber.com PDF, which was blocked; read from the City of Hendersonville-hosted copy at source_url via WebFetch text extraction). GAPS: Executive Summary table 'Housing Gaps by Tenure and County - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)' (pp. II-14 to II-17), columns: Rental Housing Gap [Total Rental Gap | Share of State | Gap to Renter Households Ratio], For-Sale Housing Gap [Total For-Sale Gap | Share of State | Gap to Owner Households Ratio], Total Housing Gap [Total Gap | Share of State | Gap to Total Households Ratio]; source line 'ESRI and Bowen National Research'. Each gap number was read twice in separately worded fetches and matched. HOUSEHOLDS: Section III.F table 'Total Households' (p. III-23), columns: 2010 Census | 2020 Census | Change 2010-2020 (Number, Percent) | 2024 Estimated | Change 2020-2024 (Number, Percent) | 2029 Projected | Change 2024-2029 (Number, Percent). households_2024 = '2024 Estimated', households_2029 = '2029 Projected', hh_growth_pct = 'Change 2024-2029 Percent' as printed. Renter/owner household counts from Section III 'Households by Tenure' table (Renter-Occupied / Owner-Occupied, 2024 and 2029 Number). GAP BY INCOME: Section V tables 'Overall Rental Housing Gaps - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)' and 'Overall For-Sale Housing Gaps - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)', column group 'Number of Units Needed by Household Income Level' with bands <30%, 31%-50%, 51%-80%, 81%-120%, 121%-150%, 151%+ (percent of Area Median Income), then Total Units | Share of State | Gap to Renter/Owner Household Ratio. NOTE: forsale_gap_by_price is keyed by these AMI bands, NOT dollar price bands - the for-sale gap table is organised by income; county-specific dollar price ranges for each band exist only in Addendum A ('[COUNTY] COUNTY Housing Gap Estimates by Income (2024 to 2029)', pp. A-1 to A-14) and were not extracted. VACANCY: Section IV table 'Surveyed Multifamily Rental Housing Supply by County', column 'Overall Vacancy Rate' (other columns: Projects Surveyed | Total Units | Vacant Units | Vacancy Rate by Type: Market-Rate, Tax Credit, Government Subsidized | Wait Lists by Type). null = county printed with 0 projects surveyed and dashes. Several 0.0% values rest on very small samples (e.g. Alleghany 1 project/49 units, Bladen 2/44, Caswell 3/110). FOR-SALE: Section IV table 'Available For-Sale Housing by County (As of Early July 2024)', columns: Total Available Units | % Share of State Total | Availability Rate | Average List Price | Median List Price | Average Days on Market | Average Year Built. Availability rate is described as 'the comparison of available units to overall owner-occupied housing supply'. CHECKS PASSED for all 26 counties: rental+for-sale = total; six income bands sum to the rental and for-sale totals; renter+owner households = total households (2024 and 2029); printed growth % reproduces from the printed household counts; printed gap-to-household ratios reproduce when the gap is divided by the 2029 PROJECTED households (renter, owner, total), not 2024 - the report does not state the denominator, this is inferred from the arithmetic. Extra fields beyond the requested schema (gap_to_*_ratio_pct, renter/owner households) are copied from the same tables. Report caveats: gap estimates do not account for Hurricane Helene impacts in western NC; the Executive Summary text gives the statewide for-sale gap as 422,118 in one place while the tables show 442,118.",
